1
00:01:51,381 --> 00:01:53,051
I'm so cold.

2
00:01:53,461 --> 00:01:54,631
Got any booze?

3
00:02:06,271 --> 00:02:07,941
A Gamble

4
00:02:08,021 --> 00:02:11,061
It's already autumn.

5
00:02:11,861 --> 00:02:14,781
Everything tastes good in autumn.

6
00:02:15,071 --> 00:02:19,491
Especially fish. Cod, trout, and herring!

7
00:02:20,071 --> 00:02:23,741
The pigs and sheep fatten up too, captain.

8
00:02:23,831 --> 00:02:25,871
That's right. It's great.

9
00:02:25,951 --> 00:02:30,461
I want some salted sausage
with some dark beer!

10
00:02:30,541 --> 00:02:32,291
Give me some.

11
00:02:32,381 --> 00:02:34,041
At first, I thought it was weird.

12
00:02:34,131 --> 00:02:36,881
But I got used to English beer.

13
00:02:36,961 --> 00:02:39,631
I like cheese with my beer.

14
00:02:39,881 --> 00:02:42,141
Cheddar had great cheese.

15
00:02:42,801 --> 00:02:44,761
Enough about food.
It's all about the women!

16
00:02:45,101 --> 00:02:48,391
The women here are so classy.
They're exactly my type!

17
00:02:48,481 --> 00:02:50,271
I know what you mean! They've got modesty.

18
00:02:50,351 --> 00:02:51,561
YOU MUST NOT COMMIT ADULTERY

19
00:02:51,651 --> 00:02:53,401
Maybe it's because they're Christian.

20
00:02:53,691 --> 00:02:56,191
Christianity is nice.

21
00:02:56,281 --> 00:02:59,151
It's popular these days. Maybe I should convert.

22
00:02:59,241 --> 00:03:00,911
I don't want to convert.

23
00:03:01,451 --> 00:03:04,831
If you're Christian, they're always telling
you not to do this or that.

24
00:03:05,331 --> 00:03:09,161
I saw a statue of the guy they worship
in London.

25
00:03:09,461 --> 00:03:11,921
He looked so weak.

26
00:03:12,001 --> 00:03:15,041
-You'll get punished for saying that!
-Yeah!

27
00:03:15,711 --> 00:03:17,671
He's so skinny.

28
00:03:17,761 --> 00:03:20,931
Thor could knock him out with his hammer
in an instant!

29
00:03:21,301 --> 00:03:24,181
I heard he's a magician.

30
00:03:24,261 --> 00:03:27,061
He does things like walking on water
and making more bread appear.

31
00:03:27,471 --> 00:03:29,311
That's some lame magic.

32
00:03:29,391 --> 00:03:32,941
Odin and Thor are better.

33
00:03:33,021 --> 00:03:34,651
Well, well.

34
00:03:34,731 --> 00:03:38,111
There's no need to jump to conclusions.

35
00:03:38,401 --> 00:03:42,571
Let's ask a Christian directly.

36
00:03:43,071 --> 00:03:44,451
Hey!

37
00:03:44,871 --> 00:03:46,331
Prince!

38
00:03:47,331 --> 00:03:50,411
Who do you think is better?

39
00:03:50,501 --> 00:03:52,831
Jesus, or the gods in Asgard?

40
00:03:56,041 --> 00:03:57,211
Well?

41
00:03:57,711 --> 00:03:59,591
I wonder what's wrong?

42
00:04:00,421 --> 00:04:04,091
Are you too shy to talk in front of everyone?

43
00:04:06,761 --> 00:04:08,851
Don't get so full of yourself, Thorkell!

44
00:04:09,311 --> 00:04:10,851
You infidel!

45
00:04:11,181 --> 00:04:14,141
Do you understand what you're doing?

46
00:04:14,231 --> 00:04:18,481
How dare you talk to
His Highness Canute with such impudence?

47
00:04:20,731 --> 00:04:22,531
Well,

48
00:04:22,611 --> 00:04:25,111
I don't like taking hostages either.

49
00:04:25,201 --> 00:04:26,321
But...

50
00:04:26,411 --> 00:04:28,951
King Sweyn is ignoring me.

51
00:04:29,581 --> 00:04:34,581
So, I thought maybe he'd notice me
if I captured the prince.

52
00:04:35,501 --> 00:04:39,091
I wish you'd try and understand how hurt I feel.

53
00:04:39,381 --> 00:04:42,461
Captain! You sound like a maiden in love.

54
00:04:42,551 --> 00:04:43,421
Yes!

55
00:04:43,511 --> 00:04:45,011
That's exactly it!

56
00:04:45,091 --> 00:04:48,431
I've fallen for King Sweyn.

57
00:04:48,511 --> 00:04:50,221
You're huge for a girl.

58
00:04:50,311 --> 00:04:52,471
You're the king of the Northern Sea,
after all!

59
00:04:52,561 --> 00:04:54,981
You really fell for him.

60
00:04:57,481 --> 00:04:59,651
You guys are all crazy.

61
00:04:59,731 --> 00:05:01,901
You know nothing but war.

62
00:05:02,651 --> 00:05:04,531
You're all going to die.

63
00:05:04,611 --> 00:05:05,861
How can 500 men

64
00:05:05,951 --> 00:05:09,701
defeat the Army of Denmark
and its 16,000 soldiers?

65
00:05:10,411 --> 00:05:12,081
We're not going to die.

66
00:05:12,161 --> 00:05:14,041
And we won't have a problem winning, Ragnar.

67
00:05:15,291 --> 00:05:18,251
You've been under the influence of Christianity
for a long time.

68
00:05:18,331 --> 00:05:20,501
Have you forgotten about...

69
00:05:21,501 --> 00:05:23,671
the honor of

70
00:05:23,761 --> 00:05:25,721
a Norman warrior?

71
00:05:28,141 --> 00:05:29,391
You mean Valhalla?

72
00:05:30,391 --> 00:05:31,641
That's right.

73
00:05:32,971 --> 00:05:34,641
The Valkyries

74
00:05:34,731 --> 00:05:37,771
are always on the lookout
for the souls of heroes.

75
00:05:37,981 --> 00:05:42,901
Heroes who deserve to be called
Einherjar, the warriors of the gods.

76
00:05:43,861 --> 00:05:45,781
Only those who have fought

77
00:05:45,861 --> 00:05:47,951
and died

78
00:05:48,031 --> 00:05:51,031
are allowed to live in the hall of warriors
in heaven.

79
00:05:55,161 --> 00:05:56,711
It's how you fight,

80
00:05:56,791 --> 00:05:58,961
and how you die.

81
00:05:59,041 --> 00:06:00,501
That's what matters.

82
00:06:01,501 --> 00:06:03,921
The stronger the enemy, the better.

83
00:06:06,971 --> 00:06:08,341
You're so old-fashioned.

84
00:06:08,721 --> 00:06:09,591
Is that so?

85
00:06:09,681 --> 00:06:13,221
It's because you're always running around
from battlefield to battlefield.

86
00:06:14,261 --> 00:06:15,971
You poor thing.

87
00:06:16,391 --> 00:06:18,731
You're just a child, Thorkell.

88
00:06:18,811 --> 00:06:20,191
You don't know anything

89
00:06:20,941 --> 00:06:22,441
about the royal court,

90
00:06:22,521 --> 00:06:24,781
about King Sweyn,

91
00:06:24,861 --> 00:06:27,861
or about my prince, Canute.

92
00:06:29,611 --> 00:06:31,241
So?

93
00:06:31,321 --> 00:06:32,281
What do you mean?

94
00:06:36,371 --> 00:06:37,501
I can see him!

95
00:06:38,291 --> 00:06:41,001
Lord! It's you!

96
00:06:41,081 --> 00:06:43,041
-He's out of booze!
-I'm your disciple!

97
00:06:43,541 --> 00:06:45,381
-I'm right here!
-Priest! Priest!

98
00:06:45,461 --> 00:06:46,421
Please sit down!

99
00:06:47,091 --> 00:06:48,261
Get him some booze!

100
00:06:48,341 --> 00:06:49,761
-Open my eyes!
-Hurry!

101
00:06:49,841 --> 00:06:51,591
Get him something strong!

102
00:06:51,681 --> 00:06:54,431
Show me your love!

103
00:07:00,021 --> 00:07:01,851
It's always so funny!

104
00:07:02,521 --> 00:07:05,481
Incredible! It must be hard being Christian!

105
00:07:06,861 --> 00:07:07,901
Hey!

106
00:07:07,991 --> 00:07:09,111
Priest!

107
00:07:09,571 --> 00:07:11,201
What do you think?

108
00:07:11,281 --> 00:07:13,031
Jesus, or our god?

109
00:07:13,121 --> 00:07:14,491
Which one's better?

110
00:07:18,661 --> 00:07:20,871
Whichever one made booze.

111
00:07:24,711 --> 00:07:26,671
You're right!

112
00:07:26,751 --> 00:07:28,671
The booze will save us!

113
00:07:28,761 --> 00:07:31,051
Nice one, Christian!

114
00:07:46,771 --> 00:07:47,771
What's wrong?

115
00:07:47,861 --> 00:07:49,821
Why did you all stop?

116
00:07:50,191 --> 00:07:51,241
Captain.

117
00:07:56,451 --> 00:07:57,621
Right.

118
00:07:59,081 --> 00:08:01,331
Right about there!

119
00:08:08,801 --> 00:08:10,761
There they are!

120
00:08:10,841 --> 00:08:12,671
It's an ambush! The hill on the right!

121
00:08:15,051 --> 00:08:16,261
Damn!

122
00:08:16,351 --> 00:08:17,641
Thorkell!

123
00:08:17,721 --> 00:08:19,471
We've got you surrounded!

124
00:08:20,471 --> 00:08:24,231
We're Ragnar's troops, under Prince Canute!
We're 2000 strong!

125
00:08:25,601 --> 00:08:26,981
It's my men!

126
00:08:27,691 --> 00:08:28,981
Two thousand strong?

127
00:08:29,271 --> 00:08:32,031
It's usually a bluff when they announce it themselves.

128
00:08:32,111 --> 00:08:32,991
Hey.

129
00:08:33,071 --> 00:08:35,241
Yeah, I know.

130
00:08:35,701 --> 00:08:39,911
This is your last chance, you rebels.

131
00:08:39,991 --> 00:08:43,121
Release His Highness and Ragnar at once!

132
00:08:43,211 --> 00:08:45,621
If you do, we shall spare you this time.

133
00:08:46,671 --> 00:08:49,631
Think carefully about where you stand!

134
00:08:50,091 --> 00:08:51,171
You scoundrels...

135
00:08:51,261 --> 00:08:53,341
You have no...

136
00:08:53,421 --> 00:08:54,631
No...

137
00:08:54,721 --> 00:08:55,631
choice...

138
00:08:57,431 --> 00:08:58,851
Your Highness!

139
00:08:58,931 --> 00:09:00,391
Ragnar!

140
00:09:00,471 --> 00:09:02,771
Good. Very good.

141
00:09:02,851 --> 00:09:05,021
You're more honest than I thought.

142
00:09:06,351 --> 00:09:08,771
Followers of Ragnar!

143
00:09:08,861 --> 00:09:10,521
Thanks for your hard work.

144
00:09:10,981 --> 00:09:12,441
I will return His Highness

145
00:09:12,531 --> 00:09:15,401
Canute to you!

146
00:09:15,491 --> 00:09:18,411
There's no need to hesitate.

147
00:09:18,911 --> 00:09:20,031
Now then...

148
00:09:20,121 --> 00:09:22,541
show us your best attack!

149
00:09:22,621 --> 00:09:23,791
What?

150
00:09:25,331 --> 00:09:26,871
You bastard!

151
00:09:29,211 --> 00:09:30,041
Stop.

152
00:09:30,421 --> 00:09:31,551
Control yourself.

153
00:09:31,631 --> 00:09:33,171
We retreat!

154
00:09:33,261 --> 00:09:37,181
But there's no need to retreat as a warrior!

155
00:09:37,841 --> 00:09:39,431
They're not running away,

156
00:09:39,511 --> 00:09:41,601
and they don't fear imprisonment.

157
00:09:41,681 --> 00:09:42,931
If we retreat now...

158
00:09:43,021 --> 00:09:44,561
If we retreat now,

159
00:09:44,641 --> 00:09:46,941
we'd be called cowards.

160
00:09:47,391 --> 00:09:49,021
There is a reason for retreat.

161
00:09:49,101 --> 00:09:52,651
We must prioritize His Highness' safety!

162
00:09:52,731 --> 00:09:56,071
Victory means saving His Highness!

163
00:09:58,161 --> 00:10:01,201
Hey! What's wrong, guys?

164
00:10:01,281 --> 00:10:05,001
Are you scared? Even with 2000?

165
00:10:05,751 --> 00:10:07,211
Or is it something else?

166
00:10:07,791 --> 00:10:12,131
"We had to hold back because they had a hostage."

167
00:10:12,211 --> 00:10:13,551
Would it be easier

168
00:10:13,631 --> 00:10:16,211
to use an excuse like that?

169
00:10:16,301 --> 00:10:18,051
You bastard!

170
00:10:18,131 --> 00:10:19,381
How dare you?

171
00:10:19,471 --> 00:10:21,051
Stop!

172
00:10:21,141 --> 00:10:22,601
Didn't you hear my order?

173
00:10:23,061 --> 00:10:26,481
Don't let those war-hungry idiots provoke you!

174
00:10:28,441 --> 00:10:29,941
Sorry, sorry.

175
00:10:30,021 --> 00:10:30,981
Was what I said...

176
00:10:31,941 --> 00:10:34,151
the truth?

177
00:10:34,571 --> 00:10:36,651
How dare you?

178
00:10:36,741 --> 00:10:39,741
I'm sending you all to Valhalla!

179
00:10:41,031 --> 00:10:42,411
If you can,

180
00:10:42,491 --> 00:10:44,241
be my guest!

181
00:10:52,541 --> 00:10:53,461
Movement.

182
00:10:53,541 --> 00:10:55,461
They've started.

183
00:10:56,881 --> 00:10:58,921
Anyone could hear that.

184
00:11:00,511 --> 00:11:01,801
The wind's good.

185
00:11:02,391 --> 00:11:04,221
All right! Men!

186
00:11:04,301 --> 00:11:06,471
Let's do this just like we planned!

187
00:11:06,561 --> 00:11:07,601
Yeah!

188
00:11:24,701 --> 00:11:28,161
You idiots! Protect His Highness!

189
00:11:30,041 --> 00:11:32,671
This is turning out
the same way London did!

190
00:11:32,751 --> 00:11:34,581
Retreat!

191
00:11:34,671 --> 00:11:36,421
There's still time!

192
00:11:41,341 --> 00:11:43,091
Two thousand?
What are they talking about?

193
00:11:43,591 --> 00:11:45,471
They only have 400 max.

194
00:11:46,101 --> 00:11:49,021
This will be over in half an hour.

195
00:11:54,061 --> 00:11:55,311
What's wrong, captain?

196
00:11:56,731 --> 00:11:58,651
Don't you smell something?

197
00:11:58,731 --> 00:12:00,691
Something other than blood.

198
00:12:02,861 --> 00:12:04,571
You're right.

199
00:12:04,661 --> 00:12:05,871
I can't smell anything.

200
00:12:05,951 --> 00:12:07,871
It's the smell of intestines?

201
00:12:07,951 --> 00:12:08,871
No.

202
00:12:08,951 --> 00:12:10,501
It's upwind.

203
00:12:10,581 --> 00:12:12,371
The smell of charcoal.

204
00:12:19,341 --> 00:12:20,761
Charcoal?

205
00:12:31,021 --> 00:12:33,021
Hey! Get me some oil!

206
00:12:33,101 --> 00:12:34,941
Don't be so slow!

207
00:12:35,021 --> 00:12:36,021
Hurry!

208
00:12:36,101 --> 00:12:37,691
All right! That's good!

209
00:12:37,771 --> 00:12:38,941
Light it!

210
00:12:55,831 --> 00:12:57,541
This is bad.

211
00:12:57,631 --> 00:13:00,341
Captain! Where are you?

212
00:13:01,711 --> 00:13:02,711
Right here.

213
00:13:03,801 --> 00:13:04,841
We're in trouble.

214
00:13:04,931 --> 00:13:07,181
We're in the middle of an inferno!

215
00:13:07,261 --> 00:13:09,471
With all this smoke, we can't tell who's who.

216
00:13:09,761 --> 00:13:11,851
We can't fight like this.

217
00:13:12,221 --> 00:13:13,811
It's better downwind.

218
00:13:13,891 --> 00:13:14,731
Let's go.

219
00:13:15,271 --> 00:13:18,231
Dying in a forest fire won't get you to Valhalla.

220
00:13:18,311 --> 00:13:20,191
This isn't a forest fire.

221
00:13:21,191 --> 00:13:22,531
Someone set it on fire.

222
00:13:26,701 --> 00:13:29,201
It wasn't them.

223
00:13:30,201 --> 00:13:34,161
They wouldn't burn themselves
when they're here trying to save the prince.

224
00:13:35,291 --> 00:13:36,461
That means...

225
00:13:40,921 --> 00:13:43,211
A third party...

226
00:13:43,301 --> 00:13:44,511
is involved.

227
00:13:47,301 --> 00:13:48,761
It's burning.

228
00:13:49,091 --> 00:13:51,601
It hasn't rained in a few days.

229
00:13:54,681 --> 00:13:56,021
Horrible.

230
00:13:56,101 --> 00:13:57,891
There's a lot of ways to die.

231
00:13:57,981 --> 00:13:59,651
But I wouldn't want to die like that.

232
00:13:59,731 --> 00:14:01,111
Exactly.

233
00:14:01,191 --> 00:14:03,531
It's a painful and boring way to die.

234
00:14:04,191 --> 00:14:08,361
It'd help us out a lot if Thorkell died in this fire.

235
00:14:08,451 --> 00:14:11,281
That monster would never die from a tiny fire like this.

236
00:14:11,371 --> 00:14:13,581
I just want to confuse them for a while.

237
00:14:13,661 --> 00:14:14,541
Thorfinn!

238
00:14:15,621 --> 00:14:16,451
All right!

239
00:14:16,541 --> 00:14:17,541
Pour some water on him!

240
00:14:24,881 --> 00:14:27,381
You saw the prince from far away, right?

241
00:14:27,471 --> 00:14:29,551
He has a helmet with a feather and red cape.

242
00:14:29,631 --> 00:14:30,591
Don't get it wrong.

243
00:14:32,391 --> 00:14:34,011
All right. Go!

244
00:14:42,231 --> 00:14:43,651
Hey, Askeladd.

245
00:14:45,901 --> 00:14:49,821
Maybe we should have joined Ragnar's 400 men.

246
00:14:50,531 --> 00:14:53,831
Combined with our 100, we'd be even against Thorkell.

247
00:14:54,331 --> 00:14:55,991
We can't win being even.

248
00:14:56,911 --> 00:14:58,541
Even if we won,

249
00:14:58,751 --> 00:15:01,501
Ragnar's men would take the prize.

250
00:15:01,831 --> 00:15:03,841
-It's a deer!
-It's all or nothing.

251
00:15:03,921 --> 00:15:04,791
Get it!

252
00:15:04,881 --> 00:15:08,801
-Even if we end up burning Canute,
-It's venison!

253
00:15:08,881 --> 00:15:10,801
we'll just pretend we don't know anything.

254
00:15:10,881 --> 00:15:13,891
No one would ever find out we did it.

255
00:15:15,351 --> 00:15:16,601
That's what you say.

256
00:15:17,311 --> 00:15:20,191
You just think that Thorfinn can capture
the prince, right?

257
00:15:21,311 --> 00:15:23,151
Regardless of what you say,

258
00:15:23,231 --> 00:15:25,271
you actually trust him.

259
00:15:25,361 --> 00:15:26,611
That boy.

260
00:15:29,151 --> 00:15:31,241
It's just easy to make use of

261
00:15:31,321 --> 00:15:33,281
an idiot who's not afraid of anything.

262
00:15:40,661 --> 00:15:42,171
What's going on?

263
00:15:42,251 --> 00:15:45,421
Thorkell's not the one who did this.

264
00:15:45,501 --> 00:15:48,171
In any case, we must escape!

265
00:15:48,251 --> 00:15:50,051
Your Highness! Hurry!

266
00:15:56,351 --> 00:15:57,561
Ragnar!

267
00:15:57,641 --> 00:15:59,021
Idiot!

268
00:15:59,101 --> 00:16:02,941
What kind of man swings his sword without
seeing who he's attacking?

269
00:16:03,021 --> 00:16:04,151
Sorry.

270
00:16:04,481 --> 00:16:06,401
I was scared.

271
00:16:06,481 --> 00:16:09,821
What if you injured His Highness?

272
00:16:09,901 --> 00:16:11,401
You fool!

273
00:16:11,491 --> 00:16:12,951
Your Highness!

274
00:16:13,031 --> 00:16:14,411
Ragnar!

275
00:16:14,491 --> 00:16:16,491
Where are you?

276
00:16:16,871 --> 00:16:18,121
See?

277
00:16:18,201 --> 00:16:21,871
Smart men check first, just like that.

278
00:16:21,961 --> 00:16:23,581
I apologize, sir.

279
00:16:24,251 --> 00:16:25,381
Hey!

280
00:16:25,461 --> 00:16:27,251
His Highness is over here!

281
00:16:27,591 --> 00:16:28,591
Hey!

282
00:16:28,671 --> 00:16:30,301
We're on the same side!

283
00:16:30,381 --> 00:16:31,921
Please, just--

284
00:16:36,261 --> 00:16:39,351
We found Canute!

285
00:16:39,431 --> 00:16:42,431
-The prize! The prize!
-The prince is here!

286
00:16:42,521 --> 00:16:43,851
Over here!

287
00:16:45,151 --> 00:16:46,061
Damn!

288
00:16:46,151 --> 00:16:47,691
Damn! You're Thorkell's men!

289
00:16:48,651 --> 00:16:50,691
I'm the one who's the fool!

290
00:16:50,781 --> 00:16:52,691
Don't kill the prince!

291
00:16:53,031 --> 00:16:54,321
I know!

292
00:16:54,401 --> 00:16:56,111
We have to be careful, right?

293
00:16:56,611 --> 00:16:58,991
Over here, little boy.

294
00:16:59,081 --> 00:17:01,161
We're nice guys.

295
00:17:08,591 --> 00:17:10,211
That was close!

296
00:17:10,301 --> 00:17:11,211
A horse?

297
00:17:13,881 --> 00:17:15,431
Who's this kid?

298
00:17:18,261 --> 00:17:20,351
Why's he staring at us?

299
00:17:20,431 --> 00:17:22,721
He looks like he wants to fight.

300
00:17:22,811 --> 00:17:24,561
Are we allowed to kill him?

301
00:17:24,641 --> 00:17:27,101
Sure. He doesn't look like he's important.

302
00:17:27,191 --> 00:17:29,481
All right. It's decided.

303
00:17:29,811 --> 00:17:32,191
Die, kid!

304
00:17:39,071 --> 00:17:39,991
He disappeared?

305
00:17:52,301 --> 00:17:53,551
You there.

306
00:17:53,631 --> 00:17:54,921
You're Prince Canute, right?

307
00:17:56,221 --> 00:17:57,261
I've come to save you.

308
00:17:59,721 --> 00:18:01,181
Wait right there.

309
00:18:04,811 --> 00:18:06,141
Impossible.

310
00:18:06,231 --> 00:18:09,151
No one would come here to save the prince!

311
00:18:09,231 --> 00:18:10,311
But...

312
00:18:12,521 --> 00:18:13,941
Why?

313
00:18:14,031 --> 00:18:15,901
Why does His Highness

314
00:18:15,991 --> 00:18:18,531
never get to choose?

315
00:18:27,121 --> 00:18:28,291
Thorfinn!

316
00:18:28,371 --> 00:18:29,331
Hey!

317
00:18:29,421 --> 00:18:31,081
You're Thorfinn, right?

318
00:18:34,711 --> 00:18:36,011
Well, well!

319
00:18:36,091 --> 00:18:38,091
It's really you, Thorfinn!

320
00:18:38,421 --> 00:18:41,091
I knew I'd see you again!

321
00:18:41,511 --> 00:18:43,101
Thorkell!

322
00:18:43,181 --> 00:18:44,601
Captain!

323
00:18:44,681 --> 00:18:47,771
You guys were fighting him?

324
00:18:47,851 --> 00:18:49,351
He gave you a hard time, right?

325
00:18:49,731 --> 00:18:51,901
Thorfinn's a great warrior.

326
00:18:51,981 --> 00:18:55,111
He gave me this wound, after all.

327
00:18:55,781 --> 00:18:57,191
Look.

328
00:18:57,531 --> 00:19:00,361
If you underestimate him, you'll get hurt.

329
00:19:03,161 --> 00:19:04,581
Wait, Thorfinn.

330
00:19:04,951 --> 00:19:06,741
There's two things I want to ask you.

331
00:19:08,371 --> 00:19:11,501
You guys are behind this fire, right?

332
00:19:14,341 --> 00:19:15,251
One more.

333
00:19:16,131 --> 00:19:19,801
You called yourself Thors' son, right?

334
00:19:22,431 --> 00:19:24,471
Your father's name is Thors.

335
00:19:25,051 --> 00:19:26,811
And your mother's name is

336
00:19:27,431 --> 00:19:28,311
Helga.

337
00:19:30,561 --> 00:19:31,561
Am I wrong?

338
00:19:33,861 --> 00:19:35,271
How do you know that?

339
00:19:38,321 --> 00:19:39,991
I see, I see!

340
00:19:40,071 --> 00:19:44,161
So, you're the son of
the Troll of the Jomsvikings!

341
00:19:44,241 --> 00:19:46,581
That's why you're strong.

342
00:19:46,661 --> 00:19:48,951
The Troll of the Jomsvikings?

343
00:19:49,041 --> 00:19:50,661
He's Thors' son?

344
00:19:50,751 --> 00:19:52,421
He doesn't look like him.

345
00:19:53,331 --> 00:19:55,251
You know my father?

346
00:19:55,341 --> 00:19:57,421
Of course I know him!

347
00:20:00,051 --> 00:20:02,301
He's the only man in the world

348
00:20:02,381 --> 00:20:04,181
who's stronger than me.

349
00:20:05,681 --> 00:20:07,811
He's a true warrior.

350
00:20:14,481 --> 00:20:15,311
No!

351
00:20:22,951 --> 00:20:24,201
That's hot!

352
00:20:24,281 --> 00:20:25,531
Really hot!

353
00:20:25,621 --> 00:20:29,041
We don't have time to talk about the past,
Thorfinn.

354
00:20:30,081 --> 00:20:32,041
I'll give you the prince for now.

355
00:20:32,411 --> 00:20:33,751
Let's do this again.

356
00:20:35,631 --> 00:20:37,711
We're headed for the same place anyway.

357
00:20:38,001 --> 00:20:39,801
To King Sweyn's main forces!

358
00:20:39,881 --> 00:20:42,671
If you're able to escape me,

359
00:20:42,761 --> 00:20:44,631
you'll be victorious!

360
00:20:44,721 --> 00:20:47,351
Don't let me down,

361
00:20:47,431 --> 00:20:49,061
son of Thors!

362
00:20:49,351 --> 00:20:50,931
Thorfinn!

363
00:20:55,351 --> 00:20:56,561
Oh, dear.

364
00:20:56,901 --> 00:20:59,231
Where's Thorkell?

365
00:20:59,321 --> 00:21:01,191
Captain!

366
00:21:01,281 --> 00:21:02,571
Your Highness!

367
00:21:02,651 --> 00:21:04,151
Ragnar!

368
00:21:06,991 --> 00:21:09,031
You're with the enemy!

369
00:21:09,121 --> 00:21:10,031
You bastard!

370
00:21:10,121 --> 00:21:11,491
You're one of Thorkell's men.

371
00:21:18,961 --> 00:21:20,961
Thorfinn's late.

372
00:21:21,631 --> 00:21:23,461
You trusted in his luck

373
00:21:23,551 --> 00:21:25,471
too much this time.

374
00:21:26,591 --> 00:21:27,721
It doesn't matter.

375
00:21:27,801 --> 00:21:29,511
I didn't lose anything.

376
00:21:30,051 --> 00:21:31,141
There's more of them.

377
00:21:32,061 --> 00:21:33,601
Hurry up and take away your dead.

378
00:21:41,021 --> 00:21:42,321
Don't shoot!

379
00:21:42,401 --> 00:21:43,571
It's me!

380
00:21:43,651 --> 00:21:45,111
I've brought the prince!

381
00:21:50,321 --> 00:21:51,581
Yeah!

382
00:21:55,411 --> 00:21:57,501
Askeladd.

383
00:21:57,871 --> 00:22:00,331
Because of your reckless plan,

384
00:22:00,421 --> 00:22:02,461
my men got scattered.

385
00:22:03,251 --> 00:22:05,381
You'll pay for this dearly.

386
00:22:05,761 --> 00:22:09,431
You would have been destroyed
by Thorkell anyway.

387
00:22:09,511 --> 00:22:10,511
Be quiet.

388
00:22:11,011 --> 00:22:13,891
However, in this situation,

389
00:22:13,971 --> 00:22:17,851
I have no choice but to entrust the prince's safety
to you.

390
00:22:18,191 --> 00:22:20,021
Protect His Highness,

391
00:22:20,101 --> 00:22:22,611
and send the troops to the main army.

392
00:22:23,901 --> 00:22:25,651
I, Askeladd, son of Olaf,

393
00:22:26,191 --> 00:22:28,741
accept your request.

394
00:22:30,071 --> 00:22:31,491
Therefore,

395
00:22:32,581 --> 00:22:36,081
as his bodyguard, I would like to
look upon His Highness' face.

396
00:22:40,711 --> 00:22:41,541
Your Highness...

397
00:23:01,731 --> 00:23:03,021
Prince?

398
00:23:07,531 --> 00:23:09,861
Are you sure he's not the princess?
